          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p
            A
            %em stability condition
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"}> Bridgeland 02
            ) on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            (
            %a{:href => "triangulated+category#FromStableModelCategories"} hence
            on a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+model+category"} stable model category
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityCondition"}
            below) singles out some of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableObjects"}
            below), that behave, to some extent, like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/indecomposable+objects"} indecomposable objects
            (whence “stable”), in that a version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur%27s+lemma"} Schur's lemma
            applies to them (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SchurLemma"}
            below).
          %p
            Indeed, in the degenerate case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+category"} semisimple category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+objects"} irreducible objects
          %p
            In the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            is the bounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            on some
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+coherent+sheaf"} stability of coherent sheaves
            (“
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
            \-stability”, see Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SlopeStability"}
            below).
          %p
            In other examples Bridgeland stability reproduces the derived analogue of
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Mumford"} David Mumford
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GIT-stable+point"} stability
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+invariant+theory"} geometric invariant theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#King94"}> King 94
            ).
          %p
            There are in general different stability conditions on one and the same
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(\mathcal{D})
            forms a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
            (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpaceOfStabilityConditions"}
            below). The collection of stable objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            in general depends on the choice of stability conditions, hence of the choice of point in this
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            = succeed "-1" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifolds"} submanifolds
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(\mathcal{D})
            = succeed "," do
              %em walls
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wall+crossing"} wall crossing
          %p
            The purely mathematical motivation for these definitions is, to a large extent, just their intrinsic richness. The concept finds its meaning in the concept of stability of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            and was abstracted from informal considerations about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-branes"} B-branes
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
            due to (
            %a{:href => "#DouglasFiolRomerlsberger00"}> Douglas-Fiol-Romerlsberger 00
            ) and followups (“
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            \-stability”).
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string-theoretic
            interpretation also sheds light on the older notion of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+coherent+sheaf"} stability of coherent sheaves
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AsStabilityOfBPSDBranes"} below
          %h3#AsStabilityOfBPSDBranes As stability of BPS D-branes
          %p
            We explain here how to understand the mathematical formulation of stability conditions as a formalization of the concept of stable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+hole"} extremal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            %a{:href => "#DouglasFiolRomerlsberger00"} Douglas-Fiol-Romerlsberger 00
            (as witnessed by various reviews of the concept, see for instance
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Stellari15"} Stellari 15, slide 9
          %p
            A key point to notice is that
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            and with them most of the kinds of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+categories"} triangulated categories
            of relevance here, may be thought of as models for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            carrying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
          %p
            Specifically, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be thought of as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaf
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundle"} complex vector bundle
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            is allowed to jump in some controlled way. Hence coherent sheaves are a slight generalization of
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+bundles"} complex vector bundles
          %p
            When considering
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            appear as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
            on the D-brane.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtext object
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi E
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %mo ↔
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %mtext D-brane carrying mass and charge
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\text{object}\, E
                  \\phantom{AA}\leftrightarrow\phantom{AA}
                  \\text{D-brane carrying mass and charge}
          %p
            From this perspective, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi rank
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  rank(E)
                  \\;\in\;
                  \\mathbb{R}
          %p
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is the number of coincident D-branes (there may be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+D-branes"} fractional D-branes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+D-branes"} anti D-branes
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+integer"} positive integer
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            have a fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tension"} tension
            and hence a fixed
            = succeed "-density," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            of the D-branes corresponding to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is proportional to this rank. Ignoring the constant proportionality factor, we make this explicit by re-writing the rank as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi rank
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  M(E)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  rank(E)
                  \\,.
          %p
            In addition to their mass, the D-branes carry
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-charge
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+charge"} magnetic charge
            known from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+charge+quantization"} Dirac charge quantization
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopoles"} monopoles
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"}> D0-branes
            ) is measured by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1(E)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            reflected in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is proportional its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ch
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ch(E)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Q(E)
                  \\;\in\;
                  \\mathbb{R}
                  \\,.
          %p
            For coherent sheaves this is essentially what is classically called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} degree of a coherent sheaf
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            carried by the D-brane, we may write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi degree
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Q(E)
                  \\;=\;
                  degree(E)
          %p
            Accordingly,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            have a
            %em charge density
            proportional to
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ChargeDensity
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi degree
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi rank
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi slope
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ChargeDensity(E)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\frac{ Q(E) }{ M(E) }
                  \\;=\;
                  \\frac{ degree(E) }{ rank(E) }
                  \\;=\;
                  slope(E)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This quotient is what is classically called the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"}> mass
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} rank
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} degree
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi rank
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi degree
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (M(E), \; Q(E))
                  \\;=\;
                  ( rank(E), \; degree(E) )
                  \\;\in\;
                  \\mathbb{R}^2
          %p
            Under this identification the charge density is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+line"} slope of a line
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line"} line
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            which goes through
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            and through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (M(E), Q(E))
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope of a coherent sheaf
            %em charge density
            reveals why this has anything to do with “stability”, as we proceed to explain now.
          %p
            First notice that, alternatively, we may identify the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            and thus unify the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            into a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
          #eq:TheComplexifiedMassInIdeaSection.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≔
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi M
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo +
                          %mi i
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi Q
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi m
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mi π
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ∈
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  Z(E)
                  \&amp; \coloneqq\;
                  M(E) + i \, Q(E)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = m(E) \, \exp( i \pi \phi(E) )
                  \\;\in\;
                  \\mathbb{C}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(E)
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+phase"} complex phase
            (modulo
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(E)
          %p
            (Such unification of two different quantities into a single complex quantity appears all over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            theory, for instance also in the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+volume"} complex volume
            or the complex coupling constant appearing in the context of
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
          %p Finally to see what all this has to do with “stability”:
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetric
            theory such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring+theory"} superstring theory
            the stable states are supposed to be the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS-states"} BPS-states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+branes"} black branes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes"} black holes
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+holes"} extremal black holes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            for given
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %em maximize their charge density
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtext stable D-brane
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext BPS/extremal black D-brane
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext maximum charge density
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\text{stable D-brane}
                  \\;\;\Leftrightarrow\;\;
                  \\text{BPS/extremal black D-brane}
                  \\;\;\Leftrightarrow\;\;
                  \\text{ maximum charge density }\, Q/M
          %p
            Now it is plausible that a D-brane
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            maximizes its potential charge density if removing any part
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            of it reveals that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            by itself has lower charge density.
          %p
            More formally,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            should maximize its charge density
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi M
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(E)/M(E)
            and hence be
            %em stable
            if for all sub-parts
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e \subset E
          %p
            hence for all
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            in the relevant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            (such as that of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{Q(e)}{M(e)}
                  \\;\lt\;
                  \\frac{ Q(E) }{ M(E) }
          %p
            Conversely, this means that a D-brane state
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            can increase its charge density, hence get close to being BPS and hence stable, by forming a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound state
            to be come an
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            In the case of coherent sheaves, where the D-brane charge density is called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope of a coherent sheaf
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi slope
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} slope(E) = Q(E)/M(E)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+coherent+sheaf"} stable coherent sheaf
            precisely if for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \subset E
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi slope
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi slope
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  slope(e) \;\lt\; slope(E)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the classical formulation of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+coherent+sheaf"} slope stability
            or
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
              \-stability
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
          %p
            Of course we may equivalently re-express in terms of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+phase"} complex phase
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(E)
            induced by the complexified mass/charge from
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheComplexifiedMassInIdeaSection"} (1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+number"} complex number
            (regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector"} vector
            in the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tan"} tan
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+phase"} complex phase
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi tan
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\frac{Q(E)}{M(E)}
                  \\;=\;
                  tan\big( \phi(E)/2 \big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            But since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi tan
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tan((-)/2)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monotone+function"} monotone function
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-\pi/2, \pi/2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            as taking values in that
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \hookrightarrow E
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi(e) \;\lt\; \phi(E)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the form in which
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"} Bridgeland 02
            phrases the stability condition, see Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableObjects"}
            below.
          %p
            But the upshot is that this is still equivalent to saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is stable precisely if it maximizes its
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            = succeed "-density," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extremal+black+hole"} extremal black hole
            and, more generally, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+state"} BPS
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+brane"} black brane
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#definition Definition
          #StabilityFunction.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (stability function)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            %p
              A
              %strong stability function
              (sometimes also called a
              = succeed ")" do
                %em central charge
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            #eq:StabilityFunction.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z
                    \\;\colon\;
                    K(\mathcal{A})
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{C}
            %p
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{A})
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} additive group
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+objects"} zero objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathcal{A}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(E)
              lies in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+half-plane"} semi-upper half plane
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %mi r
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi π
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi r
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mtext and
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H
                    \\;=\;
                    \\big\{
                    r exp(i\pi \phi)
                    \\;\vert\;
                    r \gt 0
                    \\;\text{and}\;
                    0 \lt \phi \leq 1
                    \\big\}
            %p
              The
              %em phase
            #eq:PhaseOfAnObject.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi π
                    %mi arg
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi(E)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\tfrac{1}{\pi}
                    arg\big(
                    Z(E)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\in\;
                    (0,1]
            %p
              of an non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathcal{A}
              is just the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+phase"} complex phase
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              that occurs in the representation from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(E)
              in the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"}> Bridgeland 02, Def. 2.1
            )
          #StableObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong ((semi-)stable objects)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              equipped with a stability function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo =
                    %mi r
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi π
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z = r exp(i\pi \phi)
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityFunction"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathcal{A}
              is called
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %em semi-stable object
                  if for all non-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\subset E
                  the phase
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PhaseOfAnObject"} (3)
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is smaller or equal that of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                #eq:SemiStability.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≤
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\phi(F)
                        \\;\leq\;
                        \\phi(E)
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %em stable object
                  if for all non-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"}> zero
                  , proper
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ⊂
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \subset E
                  the phase
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:PhaseOfAnObject"} (3)
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is strictly smaller than that of
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                #eq:Stability.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (5)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\phi(F)
                        \\;\lt\;
                        \\phi(E)
                        \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"}> Bridgeland 02, Def. 2.2
            )
          #HarderNarasimhanProperty.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Harder-Narasimhan property)
            %p
              A stability function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \;\colon\; K(\mathcal{A})\to \mathbb{C}
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityFunction"}
              %em Harder-Narasimhan property
              if for any non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              there exists a finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtration
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobjects"} subobjects
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0=E_0 \subset E_1 \subset \cdots \subset E_n =E
            %p
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_i
                    \=
                    E_i/E_{i-1}
            %p
              are all semi-stable
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SemiStability"} (4)
              and satisfy
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi(F_1) \gt \phi(F_2) \gt \cdots \gt\phi(F_n)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"}> Bridgeland 02, Def. 2.3
            )
          #Slicing.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong (slicing)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
              (usually arising as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
              of some
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            %p
              A
              %em slicing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              is a choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(\phi) \subset \mathcal{D}
              for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in \mathbb{R}
              satisfying
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(\phi +1)=\mathcal{P}(\phi)[1]
              %li
                %p
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo &gt;
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_1 \gt \phi_2
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒫
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_j\in \mathcal{P}(\phi_j)
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi A
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(A_1, A_2)=0
              %li
                %p
                  Any object has a finite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtration"} filtration
                  by the slicing:
                %p
                  If
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒟
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\in \mathcal{D}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mn 1
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo &gt;
                        %msub
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_1 \gt \cdots \gt \phi_n
                  and a sequence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0=E_0\to E_1 \to \cdots \to E_n = E
                  such that the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cone"} mapping cone
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mi j
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi j
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi E
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{j-1}\to E_j \to F_j \to E_{j-1}[1]
                  satisfies
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi j
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi 𝒫
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_j\in \mathcal{P}(\phi_j)
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"}> Bridgeland 02, Def. 3.3
            )
          #StabilityCondition.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              %strong (stability condition)
            %p
              A
              %strong stability condition
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pair"} pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma = (Z, \mathcal{P})
              consisting of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a stability function (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityFunction"}
              %li
                %p
                  a slicing (Def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Slicing"}
            %p
              satisfying the relation that given a non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E\in \mathcal{P}(\phi)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m(E)
              such that the value
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z(E)
              of the stability function (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityCondition"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi π
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z(E)
                    \\;=\;
                    m(E)
                    \\,
                    exp(i\pi \phi)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"}> Bridgeland 02, Def. 5.1
            )
          %p
            This justifies the repeated notation of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}(\phi)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+phase"} complex phase
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#in_terms_of_hearts_of_tstructures In terms of hearts of t-structures
          %p
            Bridgeland proves that an equivalent way to give a stability is to specify a heart of a bounded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/t-structure"} t-structure
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            and give a stability function the heart that satisfies the Harder-Narasimhan property.
          %h3#LemmaSchur Schur’s lemma
          #SchurLemma.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schur%27s+lemma"}> Schur's lemma
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
              equipped with a stability condition (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityCondition"}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathcal{A}
              a stable object (Def
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StableObjects"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is either the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              or is an
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
              over an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(E) \simeq k
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1, E_2 \in \mathcal{A}
              two stable objects of the same slope/phase,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(E_1) =\phi(E_2)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_1 \to E_2
              is either the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
              or is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            e.g. (
            %a{:href => "#Bayer11"}> Bayer 11, 2.3 Exercise 1
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Martinez13"} Martinez 13, prop. 3
          %h3#SpaceOfStabilityConditions Space of stability conditions
          #SpaceOfStabilityConditions.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (space of stability conditions)
            %p
              Under reasonable hypotheses (…), one can put a natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topology
              on the space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(\mathcal{D})
              of all stability conditions (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityCondition"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bridgeland02"}> Bridgeland 02, theorem 1.2
            , reviewed in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Bridgeland09"} Bridgeland 09, 3.2
          %p
            Most work using this fact has been done in the case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+derived+category+of+coherent+sheaves"} bounded derived category of coherent sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi D
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Coh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}=D^b(Coh(X))
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a smooth, projective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} variety
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒟
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
            is
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒟
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(\mathcal{D})
            is finitely generated.
          %p
            The space of stability conditions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Stab
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(X)
            has a locally finite wall and chamber decomposition. The philosophy is that if one fixes a numerical condition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            and considers the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            = succeed "-stable" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            varies through
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Stab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Stab(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_\sigma(v)\simeq M_{\sigma '}(v)
            should be isomorphic if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi σ
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma'
            are in the same chamber. Bayer and Macri have shown this is true for K3 surfaces, and upon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wall+crossing"} crossing a wall
            the moduli spaces are related by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/birational+map"} birational map
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#SlopeStabilityOfVectorBundles Slope-stability of vector bundles / coherent sheaves
          %p A motivating example for the concept of Bridgeland stability is the following classical notion.
          #SlopeStability.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"}> slope
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+coherent+sheaf"}> stability of coherent sheaves
                )
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a non-singular,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+curve"} projective curve
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo =
                    %mi Coh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}=Coh(X)
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              In this case the standard stability function (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityFunction"}
            #eq:StandardStabilityFunctionForVectorBundles.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mi deg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi i
                    %mi rk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Z(E)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \-deg(E) + i rk(E)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi deg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg
              is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} degree
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi rk
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rk
              the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} rank
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaf
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %p
              The classical notion of the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope
                of a vector bundle is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi rk
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mu(E)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\frac{deg(E)}{rk(E)}
            %p
              When constructing a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
              of vector bundles using
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+invariant+theory"} GIT
              one needs to consider only
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope
              (semi-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+vector+bundles"} stable vector bundles
              (see e.g.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Reineke08"} Reineke 08, sections 3 and 4
            %p
              One can immediately see that a
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaf
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+vector+bundle"} slope
              (semi-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+vector+bundle"} stable
              if and only if it is (semi-)stable with respect to this stability function
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:StandardStabilityFunctionForVectorBundles"} (6)
          %p
            Thus Bridgeland stability generalizes the classical notions of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+vector+bundle"} stability of vector bundles
          %h3#OverResolutionsOfADESingularities Over resolutions of ADE-singularities
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi ADE
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi SU
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_{ADE} \subset SU(2)
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+subgroup+of+SU%282%29"} finite subgroup of SU(2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution+of+singularities"} resolution
            of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
          %p
            Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
            of the space of stability conditions (Def.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#StabilityCondition"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+category"} derived category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaves"} coherent sheaves
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X
            can be described explicitly (
            %a{:href => "#Thomas02"}> Thomas 02
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Bridgeland05"} Bridgeland 05
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BravThomas09"} Brav-Thomas 09
          %p
            Specifically for type-A singularities the space of stability conditions (Prop.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpaceOfStabilityConditions"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+topological+space"} connected
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply-connected+topological+space"} simply-connected topological space
            (
            %a{:href => "#IshiiUedaUehara10"}> Ishii-Ueda-Uehara 10
            ). In fact spaces of stability structures over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+quivers"} Dynkin quivers
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+space"} contractible
            (
            %a{:href => "#QiuWoold14"}> Qiu-Woold 14
            )
          %p
            Brief review is in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Bridgeland09"} Bridgeland 09, section 6.3
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BPS+states"} BPS states
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wall+crossing"} wall crossing
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+invariant+theory"} geometric invariant theory
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p The general definition is due to
          %ul
            %li#Bridgeland02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Bridgeland"}> Tom Bridgeland
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stability conditions on triangulated categories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212237"} math.AG/0212237
          %p
            generalizing the classical concept of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+vector+bundle"} slope
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+vector+bundle"} stability of vector bundles
            and of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            as in
          %ul
            %li#King94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alastair+King"}> Alastair King
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Moduli of representations of finite dimensional algebras
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/download?doi=10.1.1.623.649&rep=rep1&type=pdf"} pdf
          %p
            and motivated by informal arguments in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            about the “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            \-stability” for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-branes"} B-branes
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
            %a{:href => "#DouglasFiolRomerlsberger00"} Douglas-Fiol-Römerlsberger 00
            and expanded on in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Douglas01"} Douglas 01
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Douglas02"} Douglas 02
            %a{:href => "#Aspinwall04"} Aspinwall 04
            and other articles.
          %p Further developments include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                R. Pandharipande, R.P. Thomas,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stable pairs and BPS invariants
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.3899"} arXiv:0711.3899
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+Soibelman"} Yan Soibelman
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stability structures, motivic Donaldson-Thomas invariants and cluster transformations
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0811.2435"} arXiv:0811.2435
            %li
              %p
                Rina Anno, Roman Bezrukavnikov, Ivan Mirković,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A thin stringy moduli space for Slodowy slices
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1108.1563"} arxiv/1108.1563
            %li
              %p
                Arend Bayer, Emaneule Macri,
                %em Projectivity and Birational Geometry of Bridgeland Moduli Spaces
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.4613"}> arXiv:1203.4613
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Bridgeland"}> Tom Bridgeland
                , Ivan Smith,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quadratic differentials as stability conditions
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1302.7030"} arxiv/1302.7030
            %li#Martinez13
              %p
                Cristian Martinez,
                %em Duality, Bridgeland wall-crossing and flips of secant varieties
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.1183"}> arXiv:1311.1183
                )
          %h3#introduction_and_review Introduction and review
          %ul
            %li#Bridgeland09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Bridgeland"}> Tom Bridgeland
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Spaces of stability conditions
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 80
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0611510"} math/0611510
            %li#Reineke08
              %p
                Markus Reineke,
                %em Moduli of representations of quivers
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0802.2147"}> arXiv:0802.2147
                )
            %li#Bayer11
              %p
                Arend Bayer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A tour to stability conditions on derived categories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~abayer/dc-lecture-notes.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Huybrechts"}> Daniel Huybrechts
                ,
                %em Introduction to stability conditions
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.1745"}> arXiv:1111.1745
                )
            %li
              %p
                Jan Engenhorst,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Bridgeland Stability Conditions in Algebra, Geometry and Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.freidok.uni-freiburg.de/fedora/objects/freidok:9595/datastreams/FILE1/content"} pdf
            %li#Stellari15
              %p
                Paolo Stellari,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A tour on Bridgeland stability
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://users.unimi.it/stellari/Research/Slides/LucidiStabCondBeamer.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Franco+Rota"}> Franco Rota
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to stability conditions
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sJSwN-JTOr77fpIgRWfDXkidYZmrJ0jC/view"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Rota-StabilityConditions.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %h3#examples_2 Examples
          %p Discussion of examples of stability conditions
          %p
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution+of+singularities"} resolutions
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularities"} ADE-singularities
          %ul
            %li#Thomas02
              %p
                R. P. Thomas,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stability conditions and the braid group
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212214"} arXiv:math/0212214
            %li#Bridgeland05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Bridgeland"}> Tom Bridgeland
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stability conditions and Kleinian singularities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0508257"} arXiv:0508257
            %li#IshiiUedaUehara10
              %p
                Akira Ishii, Kazushi Ueda, Hokuto Uehara,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Stability conditions on
                    = succeed "-singularities" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0609551"} arXiv:math/0609551
            %li#BravThomas09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Brav"}> Christopher Brav
                , Hugh Thomas,
                %em Braid groups and Kleinian singularities
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0910.2521"}> arXiv:0910.2521
                )
            %li#QiuWoold14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yu+Qiu"}> Yu Qiu
                , Jon Woolf,
                %em Contractible stability spaces and faithful braid group actions
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1407.5986"}> arXiv:1407.5986
                )
            %li#Qiu15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yu+Qiu"}> Yu Qiu
                , Def. 2.1
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stability conditions and quantum dilogarithm identities for Dynkin quivers
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.1010"} arXiv:1111.1010
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tom+Bridgeland"}> Tom Bridgeland
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yu+Qiu"} Yu Qiu
                %em
                  Stability conditions and the
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_2
                  quiver
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.2566"}> arXiv:1406.2566
                )
          %h3#RelationToStableBranesInStringTheory Relation to stable branes in string theory
          %p
            The proposal that slope-stability of vector bundles should generalize to a notion of stability (“
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            \-stability”) of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-branes"} B-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            originates with
          %ul
            %li#DouglasFiolRomerlsberger00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"}> Michael Douglas
              , Bartomeu Fiol, Christian Römelsberger,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Stability and BPS branes
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0002037"} arXiv:hep-th/0002037
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2005/09/006"} doi
          %p
            In terms of stability (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
            \-stability) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-branes"} B-branes
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
          %ul
            %li#Douglas01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"}> Michael Douglas
                ,
                %em
                  D-branes, categories and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=1
                  supersymmetry, J.Math.Phys.
                  %strong 42
                  (2001) 2818–2843;
            %li#Douglas02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Douglas"}> Michael Douglas
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Dirichlet branes, homological mirror symmetry, and stability
            %li#Aspinwall04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
                ,
                %em D-Branes on Calabi-Yau Manifolds
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0403166"}> arXiv:hep-th/0403166
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Bergman"}> Aaron Bergman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stability Conditions and Branes at Singularities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0702092"} arXiv:hep-th/0702092
            %li#MalyshevVerlinde07
              %p
                Dmitry Malyshev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Verlinde"} Herman Verlinde
                = succeed "," do
                  %em D-branes at Singularities and String Phenomenology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0711.2451"} arXiv:0711.2451
          %p On marginally stable branes:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Aspinwall"}> Paul Aspinwall
              , Alexander Maloney, Aaron Simons,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Black Hole Entropy, Marginal Stability and Mirror Symmetry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0610033"} arxiv:hep-th/0610033
